  "final_text": "The dashboard and the alert rule both exist. I didn't open the dashboard or check that the panels render. I also haven't seen the rule run.\n\n**Data:** The logs data view has a `timestamp` field. It also has `response` (a string, so I filtered on `response.keyword`), `bytes`, `extension`, `geo.src` and `clientip`.\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-a98b9dad Web logs overview\" has 5 panels. You can open it at `http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-a98b9dad-web-logs-overview-dfdc208d7463`. The default time range is the last 7 days.\n- Total requests (a single number)\n- Requests over time (area chart)\n- Requests by response code (pie chart)\n- Average bytes by extension (bar chart)\n- Top source countries (table)\n\n**Rule:** \"EFF-a98b9dad 5xx spike\" (id `96c17f48-68b2-4528-84ce-a1ee00a26abc`) is an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs`.\n- It runs every minute.\n- It counts documents whose `response.keyword` matches `5[0-9][0-9]` over the last 5 minutes.\n- It fires when that count is above 10.\n- It has no action attached, so when it fires it only shows as an alert in Kibana. It won't send a notification anywhere.\n\nThe rule was created disabled, so I enabled it.",
